# Following Pokémon (docs/decisions.md; world party-follower.ts): the walk. Route 202 with Turtwig (a
# Platinum walking set) as the lead. It waits under the player after the warp and comes out on the first
# tile they leave; it walks into each tile the player leaves, jumps the ledge at z 810 after them, runs
# when they run, and a save and load puts it back where it stood. The Repel keeps wild Pokémon away.
party 0 platinum:SPECIES_TURTWIG 20
set state repel 250
set state runningShoes true
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_ROUTE_202 171 805 down
until idle
+0 assert state partyFollower {"x":171,"z":805,"facing":"down","waiting":true}
+0 press down
until position 171 806
+0 assert state partyFollower {"x":171,"z":805,"facing":"down","waiting":false}
until position 171 809
+0 assert state partyFollower.z 808
# the ledge: the player jumps 809 → 811; the follower walks to 809, then jumps the same two tiles
until position 171 811
+0 assert state partyFollower.z 809
until position 171 812
+0 assert state partyFollower.z 811
+0 release down
until idle
+0 assert state partyFollower {"x":171,"z":811,"facing":"down","waiting":false}
+0 reload
until idle
+0 assert state partyFollower {"x":171,"z":811,"facing":"down","waiting":false}
# running west
+0 press b
+0 press left
until position 168 812
+0 assert state partyFollower.x 169
+0 release left
+0 release b
until idle
+0 assert state partyFollower {"x":169,"z":812,"facing":"left","waiting":false}
